accelerate 1.9.0 `init_empty_weights` vs transformers 5.12 `_is_hf_initialized`
==============================================================================
accelerate's `register_empty_parameter` re-creates every registered Parameter as
`param_cls(tensor, **param.__dict__)`. transformers 5.12's loader sets the attribute
`_is_hf_initialized = True` on parameters it has filled, so for text-only checkpoints loaded
under `init_empty_weights` (verl's FSDP engine, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct) the re-creation fails with
`TypeError: Parameter.__new__() got an unexpected keyword argument '_is_hf_initialized'`.
Gemma-4 does not hit it (its `AutoModelForImageTextToText` path never enters the hook). Fix:
strip the attribute from the kwargs and restore it on the new Parameter. Applied with:
  cd /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages && patch -p0 < this_file
--- accelerate/big_modeling.py
+++ accelerate/big_modeling.py
@@ -130,8 +130,11 @@
         old_register_parameter(module, name, param)
         if param is not None:
             param_cls = type(module._parameters[name])
-            kwargs = module._parameters[name].__dict__
+            kwargs = dict(module._parameters[name].__dict__)
+            hf_init = kwargs.pop("_is_hf_initialized", None)
             kwargs["requires_grad"] = param.requires_grad
             module._parameters[name] = param_cls(module._parameters[name].to(device), **kwargs)
+            if hf_init is not None:
+                module._parameters[name]._is_hf_initialized = hf_init
 
     def register_empty_buffer(module, name, buffer, persistent=True):
         old_register_buffer(module, name, buffer, persistent=persistent)
